@NODE License "License"
@TITLE "License"


AmiPlexAmp is closed-source freeware. The binary distribution is
free to download, install and evaluate via the built-in 5-minute
demo session. Unrestricted use is unlocked via a license key file
available to supporters of the Apollo Vampire community at
https://apollo-vampire-lair.com (see Registration above).

Redistribution of the unmodified archive itself is permitted and
encouraged. Redistribution of license key files is not.

AmiPlexAmp links against or bundles several third-party components,
each retaining its own license:

  - mpega.library by Stephane Tavenard, used as a shared library
    at runtime.
  - dr_flac by David Reid, statically linked single-header decoder
    (public domain / MIT).
  - AmiSSL by Jens Maus and contributors, used as a shared library
    at runtime.
  - MUI by Stefan Stuntz, used as a shared library at runtime.

Back to @{"contents" LINK Main}


@ENDNODE


@NODE Contact "Contact"
@TITLE "Contact"


Bug reports, feature requests, full version requests:


    Renaud Schweingruber

    renaud.schweingruber@protonmail.com


Please include in your message:

  - AmiPlexAmp version (shown in the window title).
  - Whether the app is registered or running in demo mode (the
    window title shows "(unregistered)" when in demo mode).
  - Your AmigaOS version and the hardware (CPU, Vampire model
    if any).
  - The audio backend in use (AHI or Arne).
  - Steps to reproduce, if you're reporting a bug.

For Apollo Vampire / SAGA-specific issues, the Apollo Discord is
also a good place to discuss audio output.

Back to @{"contents" LINK Main}


@ENDNODE


@NODE ReleaseNotes "Release notes"
@TITLE "Release notes"


Version 0.54

Internal audio path micro-optimisations for m68k. The MP3 stereo
interleave loop and the FLAC mono-to-stereo expansion loop are
now count-down loops with pure pointer arithmetic, on advice from
Gunnar von Boehn that the AC68080 pipeline produces an ALU-to-EA
dependency stall when a loop counter is also used as a memory
index. The previous code already used walking pointers in most
places; the FLAC mono path was the one outlier. No user-visible
behaviour change. CPU load in the audio mixing layer drops by a
small percentage on classic 68k, more pronounced on 68030/40.


Version 0.53

Multi-server and multi-library selection. Plex accounts with
several servers (or servers with several music libraries) now
get a picker rather than a silent pick of the first entry. The
choice persists across sessions and can be revisited from the
Project menu via "Select server" and "Select library".

Server identity is now tracked by the stable Plex
clientIdentifier instead of host:port. The selected server is
re-found correctly even after a network move, a DHCP lease
rotation, or a Plex relay reconfiguration. The library cache is
invalidated automatically when either the server or the section
changes, so the artist list always matches the configured
combination.


Earlier versions

For a record of changes prior to 0.53 see the README on Aminet
or the project README in this archive.

